# Day 5 — Mini-Project
**Training Date:** Friday, 16 October 2026  
**Topic:** Command-Line Task Tracker Using Python, Collections, JSON, and Unit Testing

## 1. Objective

The objective of Day 5 is to apply the Python concepts learned during Days 1–4 to build a functional command-line application.

The application should allow users to add, view, complete, delete, and filter tasks. It should store tasks in a JSON file so that data remains available after the program exits.

The project also demonstrates input validation, exception handling, modular code organization, unit testing, and documentation.

## 2. Project Overview

**Project Name:** Command-Line Task Tracker

**Description:**

The Command-Line Task Tracker is a Python application that helps users manage daily tasks through a terminal interface. It uses Python collections to manage task data and JSON file storage to preserve tasks between program executions.

The project applies core Python programming concepts to a practical data management problem.

