## 4. Functional Requirements

The application should support the following operations.

### 4.1 Add a Task

The user enters a task title. The application validates the title and stores a new task with a unique ID and pending status.

Example:

```text
Enter task title: Learn Python
Task added successfully.
```

### 4.2 View All Tasks

Display all stored tasks with their IDs, titles, and statuses.

```text
ID: 1 | Title: Learn Python | Status: pending
ID: 2 | Title: Practice functions | Status: completed
```

### 4.3 Complete a Task

The user provides a task ID. The application updates the corresponding task's status to `completed`.

```text
Enter task ID: 1
Task marked as completed.
```

### 4.4 Delete a Task

The user provides a task ID. The application removes the matching task after validating the ID.

```text
Enter task ID: 2
Task deleted successfully.
```

### 4.5 Filter Tasks

The application displays tasks matching a selected status, such as `pending` or `completed`.

Filtering should return only matching tasks without accidentally modifying the original task list.

